                <pb facs="0469" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90G2/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-24T11:00:00+03:00">June 24, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 24—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Minister for Foreign Affairs expresses willingness Iraq to negotiate
                    commercial treaty with the United States on a basis of unconditional <pb
                        facs="0470" n="405" xml:id="pg405"/> most-favored-nation treatment with one
                    reservation only, namely, in respect to countries formerly included in Ottoman
                    Empire in Asia and will accept American reservations in respect to Cuba,
                    Philippines and Panama Canal Zone.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
